        "response": {
          "output": "No. The toolkit-archive skill says an active component and its archived copy must never coexist. Retirement is a move, not a copy. The archived copy under `archive/<name>/` is the preservation, and git history is the safety net.\n\nThe \"just in case\" is already covered:\n- **In-repo component:** `git mv` keeps its history, so it can be restored with `git mv` back.\n- **Installed copy** (`~/.claude/skills/<name>/`, `~/.claude/workflows/<name>.js`): the skill removes it so a stale install can't keep firing. Nothing is lost, because the archive holds the verbatim tree.\n\nIf you aren't sure it's safe to retire, don't archive it yet. The referrer guard will also stop the move if any active component still references it."
